{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"manuscript-fact-check-track","kind":"workflow","title":"Manuscript fact-check track","description":"Fact-checks a nonfiction book, long feature or report before publication in gated steps, from claim log and source requests to checking, author queries and a sign-off report.","category":"fact-checking","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["plan","verify","review","ship"],"role":["editor","writer","researcher"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["document","notes"],"output":["table","checklist","report"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","effort":"deep","interaction":"interactive","model_tier":"frontier","reasoning":"recommended","level":"intermediate","depth":"specific","tags":["claim-log","author-queries","pre-publication","long-form"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["prioritize-claims-to-check","verify-quotes-against-source","verify-citations","check-internal-consistency"],"personas":["fact-checker"]},"args":[{"name":"manuscript","description":"The manuscript or the chapter to check, with any notes or endnotes.","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"deadline_days","description":"Working days until the text must be final.","type":"number","default":10},{"name":"publication_context","description":"Who is publishing it and where, including the country, since that affects legal review.","type":"string","required":true}],"steps":[{"id":"claim-log","file":"steps/01-claim-log.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve"},{"id":"source-requests","file":"steps/02-source-requests.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve"},{"id":"checking","file":"steps/03-checking.md","stage":"verify","gate":"approve"},{"id":"author-queries","file":"steps/04-author-queries.md","stage":"review","gate":"approve"},{"id":"sign-off","file":"steps/05-sign-off.md","stage":"ship","gate":"none"}],"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"Fact-checks this manuscript for {{publication_context}} within {{deadline_days}} working days:\n<manuscript>\n{{manuscript}}\n</manuscript>\n\nEach step produces one artifact and stops for approval; later steps update the same claim log instead of starting over.\n\nRules for every step: check against sources the author or user supplies, or sources you actually retrieve if you have web access; never mark a claim verified from memory, and never invent a source, interview or document. A claim with no source stays open, not verified. Keep the claim log as the single record: every claim, its source, its status and every change. Flag claims about identifiable living people that could harm their reputation, and private details, for the publisher's legal reviewer; do not give a legal opinion. If the user asks to skip a gate, confirm once that later steps will rest on an unreviewed log, then continue and note it.","steps":[{"id":"claim-log","file":"steps/01-claim-log.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","text":"# Step 1: Claim log\n\n1. Go through the manuscript and log every checkable claim: names and spellings, titles, dates, places, numbers, quotes, descriptions of events, scientific or legal statements, and characterisations of real people.\n2. Give each claim an id (chapter-number), its page or paragraph, the exact wording, and a type.\n3. Mark risk: high (central to the argument, about a living person's conduct, health, legal or financial matters), medium, or low (spellings, well-documented dates).\n4. Estimate effort and fit the plan to {{deadline_days}} days: all high-risk claims, then medium, then sampling of low-risk ones. Say plainly what will not be checked.\n\nWrite sections: Claim log (table), Risk summary, Plan by day. Stop and wait for approval."},{"id":"source-requests","file":"steps/02-source-requests.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","text":"# Step 2: Source requests\n\n1. For each logged claim, record what the author has already supplied (notes, recordings, documents, endnotes) and what is missing.\n2. Draft one consolidated request to the author: per claim, the source needed (recording or notes for quotes, the document for a figure, contact details for people to re-interview), grouped by chapter, with a reply date.\n3. List the independent sources the checker will use without the author: official records, original studies, archives, and people to contact for confirmation.\n4. Note any source that the author says is confidential and how it will be checked without exposing it (for example the editor reviewing the notes directly).\n\nWrite sections: Source status (table), Request to author, Independent sources, Confidential sources. Stop and wait for approval."},{"id":"checking","file":"steps/03-checking.md","stage":"verify","gate":"approve","text":"# Step 3: Checking\n\n1. Check each claim against its source, highest risk first. Quotes against recordings or notes word for word; numbers against the original table with units and dates; descriptions of events against at least one independent source where possible.\n2. Set a status per claim: Verified (source named), Verified with change (give the corrected wording), Disputed (sources disagree), Open (no source yet), or Cut recommended.\n3. For people described in the text, note whether they have been given a chance to respond to significant allegations, and flag any that have not.\n4. Update the claim log and list every proposed text change.\n\nWrite sections: Updated claim log, Proposed changes, Open and disputed claims, Legal review flags. Stop and wait for approval."},{"id":"author-queries","file":"steps/04-author-queries.md","stage":"review","gate":"approve","text":"# Step 4: Author queries\n\n1. Turn every open, disputed and changed claim into a numbered query for the author: what was checked, what was found, the proposed fix, and the question.\n2. Keep queries neutral and specific; group by chapter in page order.\n3. When the author replies, record each answer in the claim log and update statuses. Accept a new source only after checking it.\n4. Escalate to the editor anything the author and the evidence still disagree on.\n\nWrite sections: Query memo, Resolved, Escalations. Stop and wait for approval."},{"id":"sign-off","file":"steps/05-sign-off.md","stage":"ship","gate":"none","text":"# Step 5: Sign-off report\n\n1. Summarise what was checked (counts by risk and status), what was changed, and what was not checked and why.\n2. List remaining open or disputed claims with the risk of publishing them as they stand.\n3. List the items for the publisher's legal reviewer in {{publication_context}}.\n4. Hand over the final claim log as the record for future corrections.\n\nWrite sections: Summary, Remaining risks, Legal review items, Final claim log."}]}
